ORDINANCE - Pursuant to Section 2.2.1, Zoning Map Amendments, Section 5.1.2, Zoning
Districts Established, and Section 5.1.3, Official Zoning Map, of the Cheyenne Unified Development
Code, changing the zoning classification from CB Community Business to LI Light Industrial for Lot
1, Block 1, Public Works Addition, Cheyenne, Wyoming (located on the west side of North College
Drive).  Anthony Reyes, Riske and Salisbury Law Firm, representing David Trefren and various
trusts he administers, clarified they support the LI zone amendment.  Mr. Shanor moved to approve
on third and final reading, seconded by Mr. Allen.  Upon inquiry, Mr. Reyes confirmed at this point
Mr. Trefren does not have a concern with the proposed LI zone, noting Mr. Trefren does have a
concern as his residence is in the vicinity, and stated his belief that the gate to be placed on Avenue
D will be located upon the weigh station property.  Upon inquiry, Craig LaVoy, Public Works
Department, stated the road (re: Avenue D) currently is not required to be paved under Phase I of the
project, but under Phase II and III it may be considered, and verified the gate/road portion will not
be for public use.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body. (#4023)
[CA]
RESOLUTION - Declaring as surplus a City-owned property located at 1700 and 1710
Snyder Avenue, legally described as all of Lot 8, Block 348, Original City, together with
improvements thereon, Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming, and authorizing the City's Purchasing
Director to proceed with the sale of said parcel pursuant to Wyo. Stat. §15-1-112.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried. (#5568)
RESOLUTION - Amending the City of Cheyenne and Board of Public Utilities Construction
Specifications and Standard Drawings, 2007 Edition.  Mr. Shanor moved to adopt, seconded by Ms.
Williams.  Mr. Shanor  moved to amend by replacing Standard Drawing Nos. 02665-24 and 02665-
15 with updated drawings dated February 2014, seconded by Mr. Luna.  Motion to amend carried.
Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body.  Comment followed on the length of the
document and allowing time for further review.  Ms. Broyles moved to postpone for two weeks.
Motion failed due to lack of a second.  Inquiry was made regarding proposed changes to various
sections within the Specifications concerning safety, sediment erosion control and storm water
management, aggregates, potholes, and guarantees/warranties.  Nathan Beauheim, City Engineer’s
office, provided information on the proposed changes; types of aggregate being required; pothole and
pavement patching by contractors, and asphalt patching requirements.  Upon further inquiry, Mr.
Beauheim explained time frames involving guarantees/warranties for asphalt or concrete work
provided by contractors, project “walk-through” and inspection procedures, and pothole patching by
City crews.  Main motion as amended carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body
with the exception of Ms. Broyles voting “no”. (#5569)
[CA]
RESOLUTION - Authorizing the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne to adopt the
revised Statement of Investment Policy.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried. (#5570)
[CA]
RESOLUTION - Amending Resolution No. 5399 pertaining to adoption of new body art
special event license and guest body artist permit fees by Cheyenne-Laramie County Board of Health
for various services and inspections.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried. (#5571)
